# Motorhead body v1: Serpent (car 04), Base body (09-remaster 9.22 phase 6, #174). Game-space
# metres, x to the right, y up, z forward. Colours `r,g,b` are the MYO face tags before the
# repaint. Design choices unless marked [O].
#
# [O] cage 204 v / 217 p (203 welded), 17 open edges (the flat underside), 3 edges on more than
# 2 faces: windscreen triangle 95 repeats 89 (the same three vertices, same winding), so the
# windscreen's middle triangle is there twice. 203/204 mirror twins; 104 edges under 10 deg, 61
# at 10-20, 235 over 20; edge min 0.040 median 0.297 m. Box x +-0.978, y 0.188-1.279,
# z -2.183..2.041; hubs x +-0.775 (PhyWheel 0.62 x 1.25), z 1.19 / -1.5.
# A wedge with a raised rear deck: two-tone paint 143 146 177 (70 faces: nose, fenders, roof,
# rear wing and the tail) and 73 103 135 (69: the sides, the haunches, the deck, the nose's
# lower lip). The 1 1 1 faces (48) are the arch tunnels 26-65 (inner walls at |x| 0.5), the
# back-facing walls 18-21 of the step behind each front arch (the "door blades"; the third pass
# narrows the step, below), the roof scoop's mouth 22/23 and the quarter intakes 24/25. The
# underside is Underred (0 0 0: 2-11); the rear wing over the deck (66-77, 159-161, 216) and
# the Grill1 panel between the tail lamps (14/17) stay as in the original until the Full body.
# Stance kept as the original's (drop 0) for the first pass.
Body bevel=0.015 segments=3 bevel_tol=0.001 smooth_deg=10 arch_step_deg=7.5 arch_clearance=0.035 arch_lip=0.02 drop=0

# [O] glass is 54 70 86 (12 faces, type 8/9: side windows 84-86 and 90-92, the windscreen's
# sides 87/93 and middle 88/94 with the triangle 89 and its duplicate 95); the rest as the Titan's
Glass rgb=54,70,86 frame=0.02 inset=0.015 tint=0.6

# [O] headlights: one Flightg quad a side on the nose's top, tag 127 127 47 (0/1, x 0.512-0.798,
# y 0.508-0.693, z 1.553-1.946, facing up and forward, n 0.12 0.86 0.49); halo 2/3 runs it from
# (0.512 0.508 1.946) to (0.798 0.693 1.553), rgb fb fe 83. [O] the lens is lopsided about the
# halo: 0.52 m long, 7-10 cm wide on the inner-front side of it, 12-19 cm on the other.
# Design choice (#174 phase 2, after the user's headlight photo and the lamps of the reference
# model koenigsegg+ccx.blend): a 9 cm deep housing under the lens, near-black, the Flightg
# texture gone, and two projector pods 11 cm across, centred across the lens over the middle
# 60 % of the halo. The pods point along the car, not along the lens (which faces mostly up):
# upright faces (chrome bezel, LED ring, dark lens), barrels running back into the floor, so
# they step back up the lamp. No daytime bar: the original's halo glows along the diagonal.
Lamp from=127,127,47 frame=0.008 inset=0.09 tint=0.45 kind=projectors count=2 radius=0.055 rows=1 span=0.6 floor=34,35,38 led_inset=0
# [O] tail lights: two Blight4 quads a side, tag 127 40 0 (12: x 0.387-0.699, z -2.089..-1.860,
# facing back and up; 13: the corner wrapping round, x 0.696-0.830, z -1.960..-1.740); halo 0/1
# runs from (0.393 0.862 -2.036) to (0.697 0.862 -1.910), rgb f4 00 00. Design choice: two LED
# bars along the lens. 13 is 20 deg off 12, so it counts as the main facet and a bar run on
# across it bends down with its narrowing lower edge; #174 phase 4 (the user's request): the bars
# stop short of the fold at 12's outer edge (x 0.697, about 0.67 of the lens's width).
Lamp from=127,40,0 frame=0.01 inset=0.02 tint=0.55 kind=leds led_inset=0.03
Led pts=0,0.03;0.62,0.03 repeat=2 step=0,0.1 style=bar width=0.03 margin=0 clip=0 halo=1

# [O] the Grill1 panel between the tail lamps, 14/17 (128 128 128, x 0-0.399, y 0.810-0.914,
# z -2.103..-1.983, n 0.02 0.71 -0.70: 45 deg, facing back and up). Design choice (#174 phase 4,
# the user's request): a louvred vent like a window blind, its slats leaning 45 deg down from
# upright on the panel (so they stand level, pointing back). Repainted in the vent faces' black
# look first, so the vent picks it.
# Third pass: the panel is curved in the tail's zone first (the boxes test the mean of a
# face's points, and the faired triangles' means sit up to a centimetre off the facet), so the
# boxes reach 2-3 cm past it; the lamps (another tag) and the deck (73 103 135) are not picked.
# Design choice (#464, the user's request: the louvres parallel to the band's level edges): laid
# on the panel's mean plane and dropped onto the curved floor along its normal, the slats sank
# towards the grille's ends; `level=1` drops them horizontally, so each keeps one height.
Paint from=128,128,128 lo=0,0.78,-2.15 hi=0.42,0.95,-1.95 like=1,1,1
Vent from=1,1,1 lo=0,0.78,-2.15 hi=0.42,0.95,-1.95 rgb=3,3,5 frame=0.01 inset=0.04 tint=0.5 kind=slats pitch=0.02 width=0.004 blades=0 spine=0.01 tilt=45 level=1

# [O] the roof scoop's top is a shallow ridge: 135 (73 103 135, n 0.10 0.97 -0.22) and 136 behind
# it a side, their centre points 63 (0 1.279 -0.472), 183 (0 1.167 -0.932) and 184 (0 1.057
# -1.339) 2.5 cm over the plane of the outer edge 62 (0.201 1.257 -0.461) - 138 (0.304 1.142
# -0.932) - 137 (0.369 1.032 -1.339): the two halves fold 11.7 deg at the centre line, a crease
# over smooth_deg. Design choice (the user's request): one flat top across, the centre points
# lowered onto that plane (63 lands 3 mm under it); the deck 143 behind gets the same flat front.
Push lo=-0.01,1.27,-0.48 hi=0.01,1.29,-0.46 by=0,-0.025,0
Push lo=-0.01,1.16,-0.94 hi=0.01,1.175,-0.92 by=0,-0.025,0
Push lo=-0.01,1.05,-1.345 hi=0.01,1.065,-1.33 by=0,-0.025,0
# [O] the roof scoop's mouth 22/23 (1 1 1, |x| < 0.228, y 1.196-1.279, z -0.47..-0.43, facing
# forward and up between the scoop's walls 79/81). Design choice: a honeycomb.
Vent from=1,1,1 lo=0,1.15,-0.5 hi=0.3,1.3,-0.4 rgb=3,3,3 frame=0.008 inset=0.03 tint=0.5 kind=hex radius=0.012 wall=0.003 blades=0
# [O] the quarter panels 24/25 behind the side windows (1 1 1, |x| 0.517-0.75, y 0.894-1.145,
# z -0.941..-0.432, facing out and up like the glass in front of them). Design choice: slatted
# intakes, like the Titan's haunch intakes.
Vent from=1,1,1 lo=0.5,0.85,-1 hi=0.8,1.2,-0.4 rgb=3,3,4 frame=0.01 inset=0.03 tint=0.5 kind=slats pitch=0.025 width=0.008 blades=0 spine=0.01 tilt=0

# [O] the front bumper is a band of flat facets round the nose's plan, folded at x 0.275, 0.51,
# 0.73 and 0.92, in rows at y 0.189, 0.229, 0.32 and the headlight / bonnet line (0.506-0.55):
# the lip, 73 103 135 (96, 98, 99, 102: a 4 cm vertical strip at y 0.19-0.23 over the
# underside, the nose's most forward part at z 2.041), a chin strip over it sloping back to
# y 0.32 (97, 100, 101, 103), and over that the nose's front, the blue 162 in the middle and
# 143 146 177 at the sides (132, 141 under the headlight, 142 round the corner to the front
# arch). Design choice (#342, the user's request): the front bumper of the reference model
# koenigsegg+ccx.blend ([O] there: the face upright at mid-height and rounded over into the
# bonnet, leaning back 4 cm over its lower 14 cm onto a 5 cm carbon splitter; a recessed grille
# of fine horizontal bars in the middle over the splitter, 10 cm of the 31 cm bumper; its fog
# lamps and side vents left out). The cage's rows move (mirrored to -x): the bottom row 3 cm
# back; the lip row up to y 0.295, the intake's top (a third of the bumper's 0.189-0.506), its
# column under the headlight's inner corner in to |x| 0.461 (the headlights' inner edges 0.512
# less 5 % of the 1.024 m between them) with the bottom row's; the chin row up to y 0.39 and
# 7.6 cm forward, the bumper's fullest line (1.4 cm past the old lip). The headlight corners and
# the arch column (the arch rounding moves it onto the tyre's circle) stay.
Push lo=0.27,0.185,2.03 hi=0.28,0.195,2.05 by=0,0,-0.03
Push lo=0.51,0.185,2.0 hi=0.52,0.195,2.02 by=-0.053,0,-0.022
Push lo=0.73,0.185,1.85 hi=0.745,0.195,1.87 by=-0.021,0,-0.022
Push lo=0.27,0.225,2.03 hi=0.28,0.235,2.05 by=0,0.066,0.004
Push lo=0.51,0.225,2.0 hi=0.52,0.235,2.02 by=-0.053,0.066,0.011
Push lo=0.73,0.225,1.85 hi=0.745,0.235,1.87 by=0.003,0.065,0.003
Push lo=0.27,0.315,1.97 hi=0.28,0.325,1.99 by=0,0.07,0.076
Push lo=0.505,0.315,1.94 hi=0.52,0.325,1.96 by=0,0.07,0.076
Push lo=0.725,0.315,1.79 hi=0.735,0.325,1.81 by=0.015,0.069,0.07
# [O] the arch column (the bumper corner's back edge, the front arch's front rim) bends: x 0.922
# at the bottom and lip rows (y 0.189, 0.23, z 1.61), 0.874 at the chin row (y 0.321, z 1.592),
# 0.909 at the headlight line (y 0.543). Design choice (the user's request): straight up, the
# three lower corners moved onto the line, so the arch's front wall stands straight (first at
# x 0.91; third pass: 0.925, with the rest of the rim, below).
Push lo=0.915,0.185,1.6 hi=0.93,0.235,1.62 by=0.003,0,0
Push lo=0.87,0.315,1.585 hi=0.88,0.325,1.6 by=0.051,0,0
# [O] The front arch's outer rim (the tunnel faces 58-65 and the fender corners on them) is not
# in one plane: x 0.909-0.912 up the front and over the top (y 0.543 / 0.648 / 0.728), then
# 0.930 at the top's rear corner (0.726, z 1.029), 0.978 at the rear (0.615, 0.885) and 0.931 at
# the bottom's rear end (0.207, 0.718): the fender swells 7 cm behind the hub, and so does the
# lip the generator runs round the rim (it interpolates the corners' x by angle). The step down
# to the door behind it (the blades 18/19, their outer corners at 0.970 / 0.929, z 0.59-0.60)
# is 12-14 cm deep. [O] The tyre is 0.306 m wide on a hub at x 0.775, so its outer face is at
# 0.928, 1.8 cm proud of the front rim. Third pass (the user's request: the arch edge in one
# plane, the vents in front of the doors smaller if need be): every rim corner and the blades'
# outer corners onto x 0.925 (front out 1.5 cm, rear in up to 5.3 cm, the tyre flush), the
# fender's side 137/130 a plane; the blades keep their inner edges, so the step is 8-9 cm.
Push lo=0.9,0.54,1.545 hi=0.915,0.548,1.555 by=0.016,0,0
Push lo=0.9,0.644,1.437 hi=0.915,0.652,1.447 by=0.015,0,0
Push lo=0.905,0.724,1.25 hi=0.92,0.732,1.26 by=0.013,0,0
Push lo=0.925,0.72,1.02 hi=0.935,0.73,1.035 by=-0.005,0,0
Push lo=0.97,0.61,0.88 hi=0.985,0.62,0.89 by=-0.053,0,0
Push lo=0.925,0.2,0.71 hi=0.935,0.212,0.725 by=-0.006,0,0
Push lo=0.965,0.63,0.585 hi=0.975,0.64,0.595 by=-0.045,0,0
Push lo=0.925,0.2,0.598 hi=0.935,0.212,0.606 by=-0.004,0,0
# Curved into one rounded bumper, both tags in one zone (each face keeps its colour, the paint
# line stays; #174 phase 2): the lower band outside the intake (98, 99), everything over the
# intake, and (#342) the bonnet's nose top 133/163, so the fold into the bonnet rounds like the
# CCX's. The intake's faces (102 and 96) stay out of it: flat, their outline a crease, recessed
# below. The folds to the underside and the headlight stay creases. Third pass (the user's
# request: no edge or ridge on the bodywork): the bumper and the front fender are one zone (the
# `Smooth` after the splitter, below), so the fold 142/154 (20 deg, from the headlight's outer
# corner down to the arch) rounds too, and the bonnet's middle 134/164 joins it, so the 9-10 deg
# folds 133/134 and 163/164 across the bonnet behind the headlights go.
# The intake (#342): the lower band's middle faces 102 and 96 (|x| < 0.461, y 0.189-0.295)
# repainted in the vent faces' black look, then recessed 5 cm with fine horizontal slats and
# upright dividers, after the CCX's grille (a black plastic grid of horizontal bars). The boxes
# test the mean of a face's points, and the curved zone above gives 102's top edge 21 cut points
# (mean y 0.2865, 96's 0.2685); the zone's own triangles over the intake have theirs above
# 0.2997 (each has a point at least 0.55 step off the edge), so the paint stops at 0.297.
Paint from=73,103,135 lo=0,0.2,1.95 hi=0.44,0.297,2.1 like=1,1,1
Vent from=1,1,1 lo=0,0.18,1.95 hi=0.47,0.3,2.1 rgb=3,3,6 frame=0.01 inset=0.05 tint=0.5 kind=slats pitch=0.016 width=0.004 blades=5 spine=0.012 tilt=0
# The carbon splitter (#342) under the new bottom edge, out to the corner before the front
# arch: 2.5 cm thick, 6 cm proud of the edge (1.6 cm past the bumper's fullest line, the CCX's
# 2 cm), a round front, fading out over its last 20 cm.
Splitter edge=0,0.189,2.011;0.275,0.189,2.011;0.461,0.188,1.99;0.717,0.189,1.84;0.852,0.189,1.679 reach=0.06 depth=0.2 thickness=0.025 nose=4 taper=0.2 carbon=1
# [O] The fenders are fans of flat facets, 143 146 177: the front fender crown 129 (n 0.69 0.72),
# 131 and 153 ahead of it, 130 and 137 down its side, 154 and 142 down to the nose; the rear
# haunch is 73 103 135: 121/122 at its front, 157 and 156/128 on top, 124/125, 145/144 and 148
# down to the tail lamp. Design choice (like the ASC's and the Resonic's): each curved into one
# panel a side, 2.5 cm triangles, every point held to the original facets (`round`); the folds
# to the door, the deck and the lamps stay creases. [O] Inboard of the crown, the ledge 151 and
# the scuttle 155 (n 0.1 0.99, in front of the A-pillar) and the bonnet strip 152 beside the
# headlight meet it along 52-179-180-3 (36, 36 and 34 deg), and 155 meets 152 along 148-180
# (19 deg). Design choice (the user's request): those three join the zone (second box), so the
# fender rounds into the bonnet; the folds to the glass, the lamp and the bonnet's middle 134
# (5 deg) are its outline.
# The first three boxes are the bumper's (above), the next two the fender's, the last the
# bonnet's middle 134 / 164 (|x| < 0.52, y 0.69-0.83, z 1.26-1.64).
Smooth from=73,103,135;143,146,177 lo=0.5,0.18,1.6;0,0.3,1.6;0,0.56,1.6;0.75,0.3,0.55;0.6,0.74,0.8;0,0.7,1.25 hi=0.95,0.3,2.1;0.95,0.56,2.1;0.55,0.65,1.9;1.0,0.9,1.85;0.8,0.9,1.5;0.56,0.8,1.65 max_deg=50 step=0.025 loose=0 round=0.1
# [O] the side panel 120 (73 103 135, n 0.97 0.24 0.08, |x| 0.842-0.969, y 0.471-0.895,
# z -1.116..0.589) runs flat from the door blade to the haunch and meets 121 along 110-172;
# the shoulder 113 over it (n 0.43 0.90 0.07, under the quarter intake) meets the haunch's top
# 128 along 68-172. Design choice (#174 phase 3): both join the haunch's zone (second and third
# box), so those folds round instead of a crease and a dimple at 172 where the curved haunch met
# the flat side. [O] Under the quarter intake and the side window a ledge runs back from 144
# (0.783 0.871 0.181): 127 (143 146 177, n 0.30 0.96) and 112/113 (n 0.28-0.43 0.9), meeting the
# side along 144-171-172 at 61 deg (127 / the light wedge 158 under the window, n 0.98 0.21) and
# 49 deg (113 / 120); below 120 the lower side 111 and the light sill stripe 110 (n 0.99 -0.09)
# meet it along 48-110 at 21 deg. Design choice (the user's request): 158 and 127 (sixth box) and
# 111 and 110 (seventh) join the zone and `max_deg` goes to 65, so the shoulder and the lower
# fold round too (no other fold in the zone is over 50 deg); the sill's outward flare 82 (51 deg
# off 110) stays a crease.
# [O] the rear bumper is flat facets too: upright 143 146 177 panels at y 0.32-0.63, 139 in the
# middle (x 0-0.389), 140 (x 0.387-0.749) and the corner 138 round to the rear arch, and over
# them the 73 103 135 band sloping in to the tail lamps, 150 and 149 (y 0.63-0.81). Design choice
# (#174 phase 4, the user's request): curved into one rounded bumper, in the haunch's zone (fourth
# and fifth box, both tags: each face keeps its colour, the paint line stays), so the haunch's
# corner 148 flows into it; as a zone of its own the fold between them stayed a vertical crease.
# The folds to the underside, the tail lamps and the louvred grille stay creases. The user asked
# for the tail's corners rounder (#388): rounded over 10 cm (`round` 0.1, like the other zones),
# the 20-22 deg fold between the rear face 140/149 and the corner 138/148 still read as an
# upright edge in the paint's reflection from the lamp down; over 25 cm it is one curve. The
# haunch's top and side keep their shape (same silhouette in the side view).
# Third pass (the user's request: the tail round the lamps convex, the lamps one with the body,
# no edge or ridge anywhere but the scoop): the tail lamps 12/13 (127 40 0) and the Grill1
# panel 14/17 (128 128 128, repainted and vented after the zones run) join the zone (eighth box
# with the deck 146/147 over them and the haunch's 144/145), so the lens and the grille lie in
# the one curved surface and get recessed out of it; [O] 12 leans 47 deg back off upright, 13 is
# 21 deg round the corner from it, the band 149/150 under them leans 21 deg, the deck 147 over
# them 65 deg: the folds between them (20-23 deg, the rear deck's 114/115/143/146/147 too) were
# flat facets with creases; the lens stood as a plate in them. The deck (ninth box), the scoop
# top's rear end 136 (tenth: the 11 deg fold 136/143 fades it into the deck; the walls' folds to
# it, 71-78 deg, stay creases, so the scoop keeps its edges), the light panels 118/119/126 (the
# eleventh; their own zone before, the paint-line fold 115/119 is 26 deg) and the roof 116/117/123
# (twelfth: 9 deg folds among them and to 126) make it one plate from the A-pillars to the tail.
# The sill flare 82 ([O] 73 103 135, n 0.69 0.72, a wedge under the side's bottom edge from
# 10 cm proud at the blade to nothing at z -1.03, folded 51 deg to 110) joins the seventh box
# (y down to 0.2), so the crease along the bottom of the side rounds too. The scoop's walls
# 78-81, the intakes, the glass and the underside stay out. `round` per box: 0.25 as before, 0.1
# on the light panels (the quarter intake's back corner 69 sits on their fold).
# [O] The band of lamps and grille meets the paint along level edges, y 0.914 (top: 41-37-34-38)
# and 0.810 (bottom: 40-36-35). Design choice (#464, the user's request: those edges straight):
# faired, each fold rounded by its own amount and the edge sagged with it (the top from 0.898 at
# the centre to 0.865 at the lamp's outer end, the bottom 0.784-0.797, steps at the lamp/grille
# seams); `level` holds the height of their points while they slide across and along the car.
Smooth from=73,103,135;143,146,177;127,40,0;128,128,128 lo=0.65,0.55,-2.05;0.85,0.6,-0.5;0.65,0.85,-1.0;0,0.3,-2.2;0,0.6,-2.2;0.75,0.75,-0.5;0.85,0.2,-0.7;0,0.8,-2.15;0,0.95,-1.85;0,1.06,-1.2;0.35,1.0,-1.1;0,1.1,-0.4 hi=1.0,1.0,-0.9;1.0,0.8,0.1;0.9,1.0,-0.5;0.93,0.64,-1.8;0.75,0.82,-1.95;0.85,0.9,0.3;1.0,0.5,0.4;0.85,0.97,-1.6;0.75,1.06,-1.2;0.3,1.1,-0.9;0.6,1.2,-0.55;0.6,1.2,0.1 max_deg=65 step=0.025 loose=0 round=0.25;0.25;0.25;0.25;0.25;0.25;0.25;0.25;0.25;0.25;0.1;0.25 level=127,40,0;128,128,128
# [O] behind each quarter intake a light panel (143 146 177) runs from the roof scoop's back
# corner 137 (0.369 1.032 -1.339) to the intake: 118 (n 0.05 0.99 -0.14) inboard and 119 (n 0.45
# 0.86 -0.24) outboard, folded 25 deg along 137-69 (69 = the intake's inner back corner, 0.545
# 1.107 -0.743); 126 in front of 118 (7 deg off it). Design choice (#388, the user's request):
# curved into one panel, so that fold is no longer an edge; since the third pass in the haunch's
# zone (above). The folds to the scoop's side wall and the intake stay.
# [O] under the tail: the underside's middle 10 (|x| < 0.5, between the rear arches' inner walls)
# rises from y 0.207 at z -1.031 to 0.318 at -1.957, then 9 / 8 to the tail's bottom edge (0.340
# at z -2.183 at x 0, 0.32 at the corner 26); the upright rear bumper 139 / 140 stands on it up to
# y 0.63. Design choice (#388, the user's request): the diffuser of the reference model
# veyron.blend. [O] There (model units, rear +y, up +z): the flat floor (z -0.408) turns up 0.22
# behind the rear hub (y 1.33) and rises 0.243 to the tail (y 1.64), steepening to near upright,
# between side walls at |x| 0.46; at 0.226 / 0.387 / 0.548 / 0.71 / 0.871 / 0.935 of the way it
# has risen 0.115 / 0.239 / 0.362 / 0.506 / 0.712 / 0.835 of that. A keel hangs under its
# middle: flat bottom +-0.05 at the tail, 0.125 over the floor, its sides meeting the roof at
# +-0.1. Here, at about 1.3 times: the ramp from z -1.75 (just behind the hub's 0.22 x 1.3) to
# the tail, 0.29 -> 0.52 along the same curve (held over the last 2 cm to the tail). Across,
# the arches leave room for the Veyron's own size only: walls at |x| 0.44 (its 0.46 x 0.96,
# inside the arches' 0.5) leaning out 2 cm. The keel (the user's sketch, #388): a U round the
# exhaust tip below, as far from it at the bottom as at the sides, 3.5 cm: its sides lean like
# the tip's (1.7 cm over its 8 cm), from x 0.061 at the bottom to 0.086 at the roof, the corner
# rounded over 5 cm (within about 5 mm of the tip's chamfered corner offset by 3.5 cm); its
# bottom 0.402 at the tail (the tip's 0.437 less 3.5 cm), rising like the Veyron's from where
# it leaves the ramp (0.387 of the way): 12 cm deep at the tail, not the 18 of the cage's
# underside.
Diffuser lo=0,0.15,-2.3 hi=0.47,0.6,-1.75 width=0.44 wall=0.02 roof=-1.75,0.29;-1.844,0.316;-1.911,0.345;-1.977,0.373;-2.045,0.406;-2.111,0.454;-2.138,0.482;-2.165,0.52 keel=-1.911,0.345;-1.995,0.368;-2.075,0.385;-2.138,0.397;-2.165,0.402 keel_bottom=0.061 keel_top=0.086 keel_round=0.03 step=0.025
# The ramp, its walls and the keel's underside (the underside's black, its shape lost in the
# shadow under the tail) in carbon fibre like the front splitter, so the curve reads.
Carbon from=0,0,0 lo=0,0.25,-2.3 hi=0.47,0.6,-1.75
# [O] the Veyron's exhaust: one tip on its keel's back face, a rounded trapezoid +-0.0525 at the
# top, +-0.035 at the bottom, 0.083 tall, its top level with the roof, a polished ring 2 cm
# proud of the face round a dark inside. Here at the keel's 0.96, its top level with the roof
# (0.52), on the keel's back face (the rear bumper 139, z -2.183 at x 0). The face is solid, so
# the tip stands 3 cm proud of it and its dark inside is 2 cm deep, in front of the face.
Exhaust x=0 y=0.477 z=-2.215 width=0.1 height=0.08 chamfer=0.016 slant=0.017 round=0.01 lip=0.009 pipe=0.08 depth=0.02 centre=1

# [O] the glass canopy is facets folded 3-15 deg apart: the windscreen 87/93 (n 0.25 0.94 0.23),
# 88/94 (0.05 0.95 0.30) and the centre triangle 89; the side windows 84-86 / 90-92. Design
# choice (#174 phase 3): curved before the glass is recessed. A longer `round` than the paint's:
# the glass reads as one even curve, not flats joined by rounded folds. The windscreen and the
# side windows were two zones, keeping the fold between them (87/86 along 145-146, 13 deg) as an
# A-pillar line; the user asked for it smooth, so the canopy is one zone (both boxes).
Smooth from=54,70,86 lo=0,0.7,0.3;0.56,0.8,-0.6 hi=0.55,1.2,1.4;0.8,1.2,0.7 max_deg=30 step=0.025 loose=0 round=0.3

# [O] the rear wing, 143 146 177: a swept wedge over the deck, not joined to it (66-77, 159-161,
# 214-216: top 72-77, back 66/67, underside 159-161, the tip's side wall 68). Leading edge
# (0 1.079 -1.59) (0.405 1.081 -1.574) (0.499 1.086 -1.536) (0.696 1.103 -1.314) to the tip
# (0.734 1.107 -1.365); trailing edge (0 1.025-1.071 -1.87) (0.52 -1.83) (0.644 1.037-1.084
# -1.762), the side wall running from there to the tip. 4.6 cm thick at the back, sharp at the
# front, 3-5 cm over the deck. Design choice (#174 phase 4, the user's request): rebuilt as an
# aerofoil on the same outline (the tip cut flat at x 0.71, where the chord is still 14 cm),
# 12 % thick with a downforce camber, its trailing edge 1 cm over its leading edge, the whole
# wing about 5 cm higher, on two struts 12 cm long to the deck.
Foil from=143,146,177 lo=0,1.0,-1.9 hi=0.75,1.12,-1.29 le=0,1.12,-1.59;0.405,1.122,-1.574;0.499,1.127,-1.536;0.696,1.144,-1.314;0.71,1.145,-1.33 te=0,1.13,-1.867;0.521,1.133,-1.83;0.644,1.14,-1.762;0.71,1.145,-1.471 thickness=0.12 camber=-0.03 step=0.025 struts=0.3,0.5 strut_chord=0.12 strut_width=0.014

# The tail's lower corner, rounder and fuller (#388, the user's outline drawn on the wireframe
# from behind and above). [O] The cage's outline there is three points: the arch's rear end 27
# (0.834 0.318 -1.957), 26 (0.749 0.320 -2.030) and 25 (0.389 0.340 -2.174), so the bumper's
# bottom edge in plan is two straight runs (41 and 22 deg off the car's width) and the curved
# zone rounds the facets above it, never that outline: 2-5 cm inside the outline asked for at
# x 0.58-0.80. The user's curve, read back onto the bottom edge's plane (the shot's camera fitted
# to the cage's silhouette, 1 cm): from the arch's end (0.86 -1.92) it bulges out to z -2.009 at
# x 0.80, -2.056 at 0.745, -2.107 at 0.634 and -2.135 at 0.523, level with the cage at x 0.47
# (-2.144). Design choice: the points of the finished, refined cage move back along z by that
# difference (a bulge of at most 4.5 cm at x 0.76-0.80, 0 at x 0.46 where the diffuser's walls
# are and at 0.93 outside the arch's rim), at the heights of the bumper panel and the underside
# (full to y 0.56, none from the lamps' lower edge 0.81 up, so the lamps and the grille stay
# where they are) and from the arch's rear wall back (none forward of z -1.78). The outline is a
# curve of 4 cm cuts, not two corners; the bottom edge lands within 1 cm of the user's curve.
# Third pass (the user's request: the tail round the lamps convex): the bulge faded out over
# y 0.56-0.81, under the lamps' lower edge, because the lamps could not follow it (their LED bars
# were placed on the unwarped lens): the fade leaned the band 15 deg further forward at its
# middle and back again at the lamps, a hollow with the lens standing out of it. The parts
# follow the warp now (`cuts::warp_point`), so it runs full to y 0.95 and fades out across the
# deck (0.95-1.06, a near-level surface moving along itself; the wing at 1.1+ stays), and the
# z fade moves back to -1.85..-1.6 (the haunch's rear end), so the lamps move as one piece with
# the corner instead of tilting.
# Two warps since #464 (the user: a wave along the tail lights' bottom edge): [O] the lamps'
# edges run straight in plan from the cage's corner at x 0.39 to 0.70, so a bulge starting at
# x 0.46 left them a flat spot there (plan slope 0.36, 0.07, 0.40 along the lens's bottom edge),
# a wave from any view above the tail. Below the lamps (to y 0.56, gone by 0.78) the bumper's
# profile as above; from 0.78 up one starting at the plan corner, its growth only slowing
# outwards (it rises 3.0, 2.9, 2.8, 2.5, 2.3, 2.0 per metre), so the plan slope rises steadily
# (0.23 to 0.52 along the lens's bottom edge). The two weights sum to 1 across the change.
Warp by=0,0,-0.045 x=0.46,0;0.52,0.36;0.58,0.55;0.64,0.7;0.7,0.84;0.76,0.96;0.8,0.93;0.84,0.62;0.88,0.28;0.93,0 y=0.56,1;0.78,0 z=-2.3,1;-1.85,1;-1.6,0
Warp by=0,0,-0.045 x=0.39,0;0.4,0.03;0.52,0.38;0.58,0.55;0.64,0.7;0.7,0.84;0.76,0.96;0.8,0.93;0.84,0.62;0.88,0.28;0.93,0 y=0.56,0;0.78,1;0.95,1;1.06,0 z=-2.3,1;-1.85,1;-1.6,0

# Every edge cut and every face remeshed at 4 cm, like the Titan, the ASC and the Resonic (#213,
# #172, #173): the bevel strips' rows and the long fans over the big panels are slivers otherwise.
# `seams=1` (#387, as the Avalanche's, #177): [O] the original meets a long edge with two or more
# shorter ones in places (T-junctions); cutting the open edges at those corners first closes the
# seam. Mesh check, open edges 3,215 -> 3,185, no new defect.
Refine step=0.04 seams=1
